From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] docs: describe updates, lost-instance recovery and the
 TGI launcher

The control plane now redeploys a service when its spec changes, checks
its instances periodically and redeploys lost ones, deploys a failed
service again once its spec changes, reclaims orphaned allocations and
can run TGI. The docs still said that a deployed service is never
redeployed and that a lost instance needs a delete and re-create.

Describe what the code does now: the Updating flow and its downtime,
the observedGeneration rule (phase Ready and observedGeneration equal
to generation), Failed -> Pending and Degraded -> Updating in the state
table, the redeploy backoff, the reclaim, the tgi-process launcher and
its settings, the instance record file and its limits, and the new
smoke steps. Legacy kind/name allocations are noted as reclaimed.
